# Spec-first workflow

This is a class assignment about structured AI-assisted development.
The process matters more than the result.

## Source of truth

- All specs in `/specs` are approved. They, together with
  `docs/plan.md` and `docs/tasks.md`, are the source of truth.
- Before implementing anything, check it against
  `docs/project-brief.md` and `/specs`. If it is out of scope, tell
  the user instead of building it.
- If code and spec disagree or the specs conflict, choose the
  smallest option consistent with the specs, continue, and report
  it under "Deviations and assumptions". Do not edit `/specs`,
  `/docs`, `PROCESS_LOG.md` or `.cursor` unless asked.

## Implementation

- Work task by task in the order of `docs/tasks.md`, for the range
  of tasks the user names. Stop only when a check fails that you
  cannot fix, when specs conflict in a way you cannot resolve, or
  when the requested range is done. End with a short summary.
- Write test files only when the user asks for them in the prompt.
- All `Item.status` and `Trade.status` changes go through
  `trades/services.py` only.
- CRITICAL: never run `git commit` or `git push`. The user does git
  manually.
